The function `__xfrm_state_delete` in this commit contains the vulnerable construct. Specifically, it uses mutable scalar value predicates `x->km.seq` and `x->id.spi` to guard list unhashing, and deletes the nodes using `hlist_del_rcu` instead of `hlist_del_init_rcu` (lines 688-691): 

+               if (x->km.seq)
+                       hlist_del_rcu(&x->byseq);
                if (x->id.spi)
                        hlist_del_rcu(&x->byspi);

This allows for potential double-deletion or inconsistent unhashing if these scalar values are mutated, which is the root cause of the vulnerability.
